<p>Notes:</p>
<p>(A)  The Company is required to record income tax expense at statutory rates.  However, it is able to use its significant income tax loss carry forwards to minimize its actual income tax payments.</p>
<p>On July 14, 1997, LTV Steel announced its intention to permanently close its Pittsburgh Coke Plant by the end of the year.  The coke plant is one of the oldest in the United States and has reached the end of its economic life, with deteriorating operating and environmental performance.  The closure will not impact the Company's two other coke plants, and there is a sufficient amount of coke available to fulfill the needs of LTV's blast furnaces. Closure of the plant would result in charges to operations of approximately $150 million in the third quarter.</p>
<p>The Company anticipates that its results during the third quarter will reflect a lower value mix due to customer summer outages.  Also, there are a number of planned equipment outages for maintenance, repairs and upgrades that will affect earnings.</p>
